Third-party software in lake-platform

lake-platform is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). This repository holds documentation,
two small Python scripts that draw its images (standard library only), and pins of the components
below as git submodules. It contains no third-party code of its own.

Each component carries its own LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES, which list every library, image,
font and model it uses:

Component          License                       Where its notices are
liquid-bridge      MIT (OramaSearch, Inc.)       each component under modules/liquid-bridge/modules/
                                                 (liquid, lake, zetta-tunnel, the sidecars, and k0s, a
                                                 fork under its upstream Apache-2.0 license)
zetta-bridge       MIT (OramaSearch, Inc.)       each component under modules/zetta-bridge/modules/
                                                 (zetta, the agents and their corpora, the models)
orama-operator     MIT (OramaSearch, Inc.)       modules/orama-operator/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
agent-experiments  MIT (OramaSearch, Inc.)       modules/agent-experiments/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
model-runtime      MIT (OramaSearch, Inc.)       modules/model-runtime/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES

Forks of third-party code keep their upstream licenses (k0s: Apache-2.0; corosio and the http
library: BSL-1.0). Model weights carry their base model's license (the base agent is a fine-tune of
Qwen3-0.6B, under the Apache License 2.0). Datasets carry the license stated in their cards.

The names and logos are not covered by any of these licenses; see TRADEMARKS.md.
